Q: How to reverse an array using recursion? A: <p>I tested for <code>[1, 2, 3, 4]</code> and it gives <code>[4, 2, 3, 1]</code>. So code has problem with middle index.</p>
<p>I displayed information in function and for <code>[1,2]</code> I see it converts <code>[1,2]</code> (for index=0) to <code>[2,1]</code> and in next step (for index=1) it converts to <code>[1,2]</code> but it shouldn't run code for index=1.</p>
<p>Problem is code inside <code>if</code>. You shouldn't run it but only return array. Correct version:</p>
<pre><code>public static int[] reverseArrayForwardRecursion(int startingIndex, int[] arr) {

    if (startingIndex == (arr.length / 2)) {
        // int temp = arr[startingIndex];
        // arr[startingIndex] = arr[arr.length - startingIndex - 1];
        // arr[arr.length - startingIndex - 1] = temp;
        return arr;
    }

    int temp = arr[startingIndex];
    arr[startingIndex] = arr[arr.length - startingIndex - 1];
    arr[arr.length - startingIndex - 1] = temp;

    return reverseArrayForwardRecursion(startingIndex + 1, arr);
}
</code></pre>
<hr />
<p>Full code used for tests:</p>
<pre><code>import java.util.Arrays;

public class Main {

    public static int[] reverseArrayForwardRecursion(int startingIndex, int[] arr) {
        //System.out.println(&quot;&gt; startingIndex: &quot; + startingIndex);
        //System.out.println(&quot;&gt; arr.length / 2: &quot; + (arr.length / 2));

        if (startingIndex == (arr.length / 2)) {
            // System.out.println(&quot;&gt;&gt; inside IF&quot;);
            // int temp = arr[startingIndex];
            // arr[startingIndex] = arr[arr.length - startingIndex - 1];
            // arr[arr.length - startingIndex - 1] = temp;
            return arr;
        }

        int temp = arr[startingIndex];
        arr[startingIndex] = arr[arr.length - startingIndex - 1];
        arr[arr.length - startingIndex - 1] = temp;

        return reverseArrayForwardRecursion(startingIndex + 1, arr);
    }

    public static void test(int[] arr) {
        System.out.println(&quot;Before: &quot; + Arrays.toString(arr));
        reverseArrayForwardRecursion(0, arr);
        System.out.println(&quot;After:  &quot; + Arrays.toString(arr));
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr1 = { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };
        test(arr1);

        int[] arr2 = { 1, 2 };
        test(arr2);

        int[] arr3 = { 1, 2, 3, 4 };
        test(arr3);
    }
}
</code></pre>
